# {{.Type}}: {{.Name}}

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

~> This resource owns the complete ordered firewall ruleset for the VNet. Import a VNet with existing
rules before managing it; creating this resource will not overwrite unowned rules.

VNet firewall rules apply to forwarded traffic. Proxmox VE does not allow `REJECT` on a forward chain,
so direct rules support the `ACCEPT` and `DROP` actions. A rule can instead reference a cluster security
group with `security_group`.

The VNet must be present in the active SDN configuration before its firewall API becomes available. Use
`proxmox_sdn_applier` after creating the VNet, and make this resource depend on that applier.

